===== T3c2 ORDERING HAZARD (shared constant appended LAST into the repair engine) =====
{
  "repair_options_string": "-c statement_timeout=60000 -c lock_timeout=10000 -c idle_in_transaction_session_timeout=60000 -c timezone=UTC -c application_name=ensemble-manager",
  "backends_by_application_name": {
    "ensemble-manager": 1
  },
  "repair_engine_reports_manager_name": true,
  "verdict": "CONFIRMED HAZARD: the repair engine reports the manager's application_name because the shared constant is appended LAST"
}

===== T3c3 LAST -c WINS within a single options string =====
{
  "A_then_B": "beta",
  "B_then_A": "alpha"
}

===== T3c4 conninfo application_name vs options -c application_name =====
{
  "results": {
    "conninfo_only": "from-conninfo",
    "options_only": "from-options",
    "both": "from-conninfo"
  },
  "verdict": "MEASURED: the conninfo application_name parameter WINS over options=-c application_name (both set -> 'from-conninfo'). So the conninfo parameter is the STRONGER channel; -c inside options is weaker. Ordering WITHIN one options string is still last-wins (T3c3)."
}

